                <pb facs="0464" n="352" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg352"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 493.11A/5.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Minister
                        Calhoun.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-10-15"><hi rendition="#italic">October 15,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Referring to legation’s telegram of October 15, Mr. Adee says the department
                    awaits report of the legation on the Changsha claims, the only detailed report
                    that has been received being a carbon copy of dispatch of June 29, 1910, from
                    the consul general at Hankow to the legation. Mr. Adee says if this dispatch
                    submits all claims, and if the legation approves them and has so reported to the
                    department, he may instruct the consul general at Hankow to negotiate a
                    settlement accordingly and to advise the Wai-wu-Pu in this sense.</p>
            </div>
